=== ArrayBoundsFlowAnalysis Sample ===
--- 1. Literal indices on concrete arrays ---
  arr[0] = 10
  arr[2] = 30
  arr[4] = 50
--- 2. For-loop with literal bounds ---
  nums = 10 20 30 40 50 
--- 3. For-loop with .Length on concrete arrays ---
  sum of [100, 200, 300, 400] = 1000
--- 4. For-loop with .Length on parameter arrays (symbolic) ---
  SumAll([5, 10, 15, 20, 25]) = 75
  PrintArray: 5 10 15 20 25 
--- 5. Nested array indexing ---
  sum of row 0 = 6
  sum of row 1 = 15
  sum of row 2 = 24
--- 6. Indexer with ArrayBounds constraint ---
  buf[0] = 11
  buf[4] = 55
  buf.Describe() = BoundedBuffer(length=5)
--- 7. Dependent-typed array class ---
  FixedArray<5>.GetSize() = 5
  FixedArray<5>.Describe() = FixedArray<5>
  FixedArray<10>.GetSize() = 10
  FixedArray<10>.Describe() = FixedArray<10>
=== ArrayBoundsFlowAnalysis Done ===
